.TH httpd 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
httpd \- a small web server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B httpd
[\fIport\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B httpd
serves files from the directory it was started in, on port 8080 unless
another
.I port
is given, one connection at a time.
.PP
A request for
.B /
gets
.BR index.html ,
a missing file gets a 404, and a path containing
.B ..
is refused.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# mkdir /tmp/www
# cd /tmp/www
# echo hello > index.html
# httpd &
1234
.fi
.SH STOPPING IT
Note the process id the shell prints when you background it, and
.B kill
that.  The shell has no job control and
.B kill
takes no job numbers, so
.B kill %1
does not work here; if you have lost the number,
.B ps
will find it.
.PP
Stop it before flashing or rebooting.  A running server holds the
filesystem open, so
.B remount \-n / ro
refuses and the card goes down dirty.
.SH NOTES
The machine can reach its own server, through 127.0.0.1 or through its
own address.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR htget (1),
.BR wifi (1),
.BR remount (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR ps (1)
